  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<h2>Assassinate</h2><p>You’re adept at ambushing a target, granting you the following benefits:</p><h3>Initiative</h3><p>You have permanent advantage on Initiative rolls.</p><h3>Assassin Strike</h3><p>You are at your deadliest when you attack a surprised enemy. Any weapon attack you score against a surprised creature is a critical hit.</p><p class=\"runyth-boundary\"><strong>Foundry workflow:</strong> Roll the weapon attack normally. When the GM confirms that the target is explicitly Surprised and the attack hits, select the standard <em>Critical Hit</em> option in the D&amp;D 5e damage dialog. This module intentionally adds no separate Assassin Strike attack button.</p>",
